{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1454111-which-hunter-group-would-you-join-irl","id":1454111,"title":"Which Hunter group would you join IRL?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-07-02T19:59:14-07:00","id":1454111,"title":"Which Hunter group would you join IRL?","content":"Here's an entertaining thought experiment. If you were to join up with a Compact and/or Conspiracy in real life which one would it be and why?<br /> <br /> I'll start. Philosophically, and because on the civilian side I'm a lab rat, I'd see myself joining Null Mysteries. I just identify with their world view the most; I'm of the mind that if something's real and observable it can be studied, if it can be studied then its mysteries can be discovered through observation and experimentation. If I can observe something and interact with it, then I can form educated guesses as to how it works, then set up a well planned experiment to test my idea. If my idea turns out to be wrong I can always go back to the drawing board and form a new idea, taking the data from the failed experiment into account. Just have to be careful to survive what can study me back...<br /> <br /> On the Reserve side though, I'm an Entomologist for the US Army (yes the army has bug experts for soldiers, you can thank Walter Reed for that). It's not too much of a leap to think that I'd be recruited to Task Force: Valkyrie because Entomologists are already studying and interacting with strange creatures. Insects; their skin IS their skeleton, their heart is along the back and middle of their butt, their central nervous system runs down the center of their chest, they breath through tiny holes in their exoskeleton, their mouth parts move sideways rather than up and down because those mouth parts used to be the forelimbs of their primordial ancestors, and the legs and eyes...insects are alien and strange compared to us. I could see Task Force: Valkyrie calling me in to help study and deal with supernatural insects or insect-like creatures.<br /> <br /> DISCLAIMER: I know that my world view can clash with others, and that there are Hunter orgs in the game whose outlook I definitely don't share, BUT I'm not trying to start a flame war, nor will I bash other people's beliefs here. I think it's against a community guideline anyway. Even if it wasn't that's not the point of this thread. This is an opportunity to think about what hunter organization(s) YOU would join, why, and share with the group for entertainment purposes. No judgement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10065-zolace","name":"Zolace","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-02T22:58:11-07:00","id":1454117,"title":"","content":"Well I assume Lucifuge are off the table because that\u2019s based on a prerequisite none of us possess? Maybe the Ascending Ones since they also believe in diplomatic relations with the supernatural, and there\u2019s a scholarship tradition that connects with my own heritage, as opposed to the other major group of occult scholars who are dealing with the baggage of what they're movement did to people with my heritage.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-03T17:14:11-07:00","id":1454163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1454111-which-hunter-group-would-you-join-irl?p=1454117#post1454117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well I assume Lucifuge are off the table because that\u2019s based on a prerequisite none of us possess?</div> </div> </div> </div>I overlooked that one. Good catch. While there are people in the real world occult/new age community who believe they are <u>spiritually</u> nefilhim or something similar like an angel/demon born into a human body (google &quot;Earth Angels&quot;), I guess since no one is <u>physically</u> half human half demon it doesn't count? Though on the other hand I guess I could see such individuals saying they'd join that group.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10065-zolace","name":"Zolace","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-05T09:46:00-07:00","id":1454285,"title":"","content":"Probably the AKD for a conspiracy, maybe Null Mysteriis for a compact.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-07T11:24:43-07:00","id":1454470,"title":"","content":"Any of the ones with nice, safe desk jobs available.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-12T21:49:32-07:00","id":1454795,"title":"","content":"Aw geez Rick, that's a tough question. One I will over answer trying to decide which one I'd go within a more complicated way than I should.<br /> <br /> Hunter 1st Compacts: Uh. Probably either the Loyalists of Thule-the stark reminder of the dangers of powers, acting as a communal support function and subtle judge of their community, the dig for occult secrets and knowing More Than Everyone Else, Fuck Nazis-or Network Zero-very much my people, let's call it there.<br /> <br /> Hunter 1st Conspiracies: The Ascending Ones or the Lucifuge-deep emphasis on compassion, insight, and diplomacy for both, deeply interesting histories, on the AO's part a emphasis on interconnected communities, on the Lucifuge, power ostensibly graspable that can punch out the larger forms of oppression.<br /> <br /> Witch Finders Compacts: Is it weird to say The Promethean Brotherhood? We've established not every mage uses their power to their best ends, and while the Promethean Brotherhood is also not all sunshine and rainbows, they still have a lot more punch against some of the more influential enemies in the Chronicles world.<br /> <br /> Spirit Slayers Compacts: The Talbot Group, hands down. Sure, they have no fucking clue what they're doing, but they're still among the better motivated of the Hunter Organizations and that makes it easy for them to learn better.<br /> <br /> Night Stalkers Compacts: Uhm. the Night Angels probably need more people, but they wouldn't trust me and also it's more work. Sister's Blood Maidenhood.<br /> <br /> Slasher/Mortal Remains Compacts: It's a toss up between Habibti Ma and Yuri's Group. Probably Yuri's Group.<br /> <br /> Supplemental Conspiracies: Is it weird I kind of want to leave my answer at The Cainite Conspiracy? It's not, it's Les Mysteres first, and then from there, barring the Merrick Institute which I would not want by virtue of having been part or and probably couldn't get into as an adult, they're all kind of assholes, soooooooo <i>maybe</i> the Cainites?<br /> <br /> Dark Eras Compacts: Azusa Miko or Bijin. Which depends on how vain I'm feeling on the day(some days I am <i>sooo</i> pretty, people).<br /> <br /> Dark Era Conspiracies': What, you mean which of the only four conspiracies that exist across three books? Order of the Black Knight, duh, it has a lot of varying levels of action, and it's highest action has you in a bitching suit of immortality armor that eats your sanity.<br /> <br /> Hunter 2nd Compacts: Wait, do I even qualify for any of the new ones?<br /> <br /> Hunter 2nd Conspiracies: Sure, I'll dance for some ghosts-it's not like there's a lot of new options outside of the Council of Bones.<br /> <br /> Actual Compact Choice: Honestly, the Loyalists are the right layer of action and motivation for me. You can have days off and take the backseat, but you can still also clearly do a lot of good, and even occasionally take to the scene.<br /> <br /> Actual Conspiracy Choice: The Ascending Ones do not get enough love-these are very much my people (that do not greet you by putting a gun to your head and giving you a very clear choice).<br /> <br /> And between the two, the grand winner is:<br /> <br /> The Loyalists of Thule. I mean, c'mon, off days, background work, AND punching Nazis, what's not love.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-13T06:49:41-07:00","id":1454819,"title":"","content":"With all the ghost stories I know of / have ready access to, likely a regional variant of the Council of Bones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-15T18:20:47-07:00","id":1455003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1454111-which-hunter-group-would-you-join-irl?p=1454470#post1454470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any of the ones with nice, safe desk jobs available.</div> </div> </div> </div>Loyalists of Thule. Be one of their librarians. They always need a good librarian.<br /> <br /> The Cherion Group, but not one of their field operatives. You'd want to be one of the R&amp;D biochemists trying to synthesize the latest prescription medicines from the monster parts the field operatives brought in. That involves a lot of desk work as well as bench work in a lab.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10065-zolace","name":"Zolace","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-30T10:53:35-07:00","id":1455802,"title":"","content":"Ashwood Abbey if any are available surround myself with the finer things in life.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-13T06:48:56-07:00","id":1456755,"title":"","content":"In terms of philosophy, Yuri's Group seems to be the most relatable group.<br /> <br /> Logically speaking, I'd probably get pulled into one based on my affiliations, and how I first got pulled in. So I could say probably one of these.<br /> <br /> 1. I do some volunteering with a local child advocacy center, which would probably have contacts with Yuri's Group.<br /> 2. The pastor and former pastor of my church are both cousins of mine, and I have a good rep in general there, which would lends itself towards being a good candidate for the Long Night.<br /> 3. My father is a federal magistrate judge, so he'd probably be targeted by vampires for manipulation. He's got a lot of integrity, so it'd show in his mental health. If something happened to him, given I have a degree in Public Administration, I might be recruited and given a job in the government since I have reasonable qualifications.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25382-tzauri","name":"Tzauri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-25T17:27:30-07:00","id":1457663,"title":"","content":"yuri\u2019s group because they are 1 of the most ethical compacts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/blob:http://forum.theonyxpath.com/30ff2a5d-ff5b-4dec-8fca-50f9a75f97ea\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <br /> \u201cwhat in the goddamn?\u201d -benny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26749-mothstrigoi","name":"Mothstrigoi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-01T17:13:43-07:00","id":1458275,"title":"","content":"As much as I'd like to flatter myself that I could join the Aegis Kai Doru, I'd likely end up part of the Long Night or Loyalists of Thule. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-03T23:00:44-07:00","id":1519709,"title":"","content":"Honestly I\u2019d say either Loyalists of Thule or Yuri\u2019s Group. Probably Loyalists of Thule, because hunters absolutely need more people who are actually trying to figure out what\u2019s going on in the supernatural world and are also up for punching Nazis on the side. Seems like a good fit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27217-skyewards","name":"Skyewards","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27217_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-06T10:04:52-07:00","id":1519967,"title":"","content":"Union, Pretty good guys, little work, get the info you need, get help unionizing my work place...<br /> It's be good.<br /> <br /> <br /> For conspicies...<br /> Merrick I guess, I heard they pay good, I dont mean as a Psychic, Merrick still needs people to sign paperwork, and own shell businesses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27385-cross-a-way","name":"Cross-a-way","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27385_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-10T06:10:55-07:00","id":1520286,"title":"","content":"The easiest I could probably see myself working with would be network 0. Gather proof but not having to directly interfere. While I might not be cowardly I'm realistic enough to not want to fight a monster head on. Plus, they would be the least likely to get aggressive if I pick up &quot;tricks&quot; like supernatural merits or the gifted merit from witchfinder.<br /> <br /> Lucifuge is a favorite of mine but I do understand that truly being such would be hell, pun intended.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}